    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d74">

                <pb facs="0168" n="94" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg94"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1729.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>, </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-03-31"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 31, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your despatch of the 15th of March, No. 1168, which is accompanied by a copy
                    of a continuation of the correspondence between yourself and Lord Clarendon on
                    the subject of the extraordinary speech made by the attorney general of Great
                    Britain, on tin 23d of February, in the House of Commons.</p>
                <p>The President is very well satisfied with your reply, which closes the discussion
                    in a manner which is thought equally dignified and decisive.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWABD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
